{
  "Title": "ELSA-2026-98560:  libsoup3 security update (IMPORTANT)",
  "Description": "[3.6.6-9]\n- CVE-2026-102558 libsoup3: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow during WebSocket\n  receive-buffer growth\n\n[3.6.6-8]\n- CVE-2026-102555 libsoup3: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow via uninitialized\n  length in data-URI base64 decoding\n\n[3.6.6-7]\n- CVE-2026-102556 libsoup3: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow from WebSocket\n  Pong signal type confusion\n\n[3.6.6-6]\n- CVE-2026-102560 libsoup3: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow during outgoing\n  permessage-deflate buffer growth\n\n[3.6.6-5]\n- CVE-2026-102559 libsoup3: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow during WebSocket\n  client-frame masking\n\n[3.6.6-4]\n- Fix CVE-2026-85197: HTTP/2 crash in on_data_read after connection close\n\n[3.6.6-3]\n- Fix CVE-2026-15711: Reject oversized WebSocket control frames\n\n[3.6.6-2]\n- Fix CVE-2026-15709: bound decompressed WebSocket message size",
